    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Tribunal has a duty to consider certain factors.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable to make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975, the Tribunal must:";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "The Tribunal must have regard to...";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/executionSurface> "modalities::logic::deontic";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/confidence> 1.0000;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/curationStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Proposed>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/asserts> <https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4-logic-deontic-2>.
